# Backup archives and their staging dirs (backup.sh output; the archive holds
# every password_hash/api_key, and build contexts are the repo root, so a
# build running while an archive exists would bake it into an image layer).
# The two patterns are not redundant: backup.sh's default name is
# backup-YYYY-MM-DD.db, but an operator may pass any path (`/var/backups/pew/
# pew.db`, `pre-cluster-*.db`, `dump.db`). A `*.db` inside the repo therefore
# must never reach a build context — verified: only the default name was being
# excluded while a `dump.db` next to it entered /ctx intact.
**/backup-*.db
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.pew-backup.*/